THE POINT OF ALL THIS: the secret is not in the file.

  the file is 187 characters, all of them hex

  contains the secret:        false
  contains 'sk-ant':          false
  contains the name it is under: false

-- and the key is not in the file either, because it is never written
  contains the key: false
  a key file exists: false

-- the WRONG key cannot read it, and does not pretend to
  ok=false status=unreadable
  (AES-GCM is authenticated, so 'wrong key' and 'tampered' are the
   same answer — and saying which would be inventing information the
   cipher deliberately does not give)

-- a locked store is not an empty one
  ok=false status=locked
  names(): 0 (a locked store lists nothing)
